Z||000000||RICK||01-06-2000||06:17 PM||||I need help (but don't we all)<BR>87 v-6, 5 speed<BR>The problem started about a week ago.  When trying to start the car it was start for a second and then stop.  I would crank the car over for 5-6 seconds and then it would start.  This happened about 4 times.  This morning I tried starting the car and it would only turn over and not even try and start.  <BR>I can here the fuel pump prime and smell gas after cranking the engine over. We disconected the wire from the coil to see if it was sparking and got nothing when grouned.  I disconected the tach filter to see if that helped and nothing.  <BR>Anybody have any sugustions?<BR>Thanks!||||reg||9
Z||000001||william_thorniii||01-06-2000||06:19 PM||||If you're not getting spark, I would put $ on the coil.<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000002||RICK||01-07-2000||09:12 AM||||When testing the coil does anyone know the primary and secondary resistance a stock coil should have (apx)?<BR>How can I check if the coil is receiving a signal to fire?<BR>Thank's||||reg||5
Z||000003||wwh0001||01-07-2000||10:30 AM||||No spark. Would look at three things. Probable cause is pick up coil, these things fry easily and if you haven't changed it recently would be best guess. next would look at ignition module . last would be the ignition coil. while the ignition coil can fail it is not as likely to fail as the pick up and/or module.||||reg||1
Z||000004||87GTBro||01-07-2000||02:43 PM||||My first guess was the ignition module.  I think it is located inside the distributor.  It's not entirely too expensive.  Should be under $50 so I would try that theory first.||||reg||1
Z||000005||mshill||01-07-2000||03:25 PM||||My first guess would also be the ignition module, second the pickup coil and last the ignition coil.<P>Some places will test the ignition module for you.  If the module tests good, then buy a pickup coil.  They are only $10-12 and probably needs replacing if you have more than 40,000 miles on it anyway.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||RICK||01-07-2000||07:10 PM||||Just an update, I borrowed a coil from my friends salvage yard and that wasn't it, I pulled the ecm and am taking it to Napa auto parts so they can check it out.||||reg||1
Z||000007||RICK||01-10-2000||10:18 AM||||Another update.. I took the Ignition module to Napa and they tested it, it was not working.  Next week she should be up and running.||||reg||10
